1790667289.339	
1790667289.339	The Morganian type was a significant innovation in printing because it allowed for the mass production of books. Before the invention of the printing press, books were copied by hand, which was a labor-intensive process. The cost of copying a book was prohibitively expensive, and it was not until the invention of the printing press that it became possible to produce books on a large scale.
